{"case_id":"C078","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics","state interaction"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["set_quirks","fuzz_complex","wuffs_json__decoder__decode_trailing_new_line","wuffs_json__decoder__decode_comment"],"reason":"H0 never enables the newly exposed WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_COMMENT, so it cannot exercise S1's acceptance and state handling for comments after a completed top-level JSON value. This behavior requires interaction with WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_NEW_LINE and either WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_COMMENT_BLOCK or WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_COMMENT_LINE, including distinct block-versus-line transitions recorded in f_comment_type.","evidence":["S1 adds the public constant WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_COMMENT.","H0's set_quirks array includes WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_COMMENT_BLOCK, WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_COMMENT_LINE, and WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_NEW_LINE, but omits WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_COMMENT.","wuffs_json__decoder__decode_trailing_new_line initializes f_allow_trailing_comment from f_quirks[17] and calls wuffs_json__decoder__decode_comment only when that flag is true.","wuffs_json__decoder__decode_comment now sets f_comment_type to 1 for a completed block comment and 2 for a completed line comment; decode_trailing_new_line uses those values to choose whether to continue consuming whitespace or stop.","fuzz_complex varies source and token buffer limits, but those suspension paths cannot cover the new trailing-comment branch while the controlling quirk is never enabled."],"recommended_action":"Add WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_COMMENT to H0's set_quirks configuration space and exercise it in combination with WUFFS_JSON__QUIRK_ALLOW_TRAILING_NEW_LINE and each comment quirk, covering block and line comments, EOF/newline boundaries, following whitespace, malformed comments, and short-read/short-write resumptions."}
